      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg once daily is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 10 mg per day. A dose that high could cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, peripheral edema, and shock. Normal kidney and liver function and a weight of 70 kg don't change that.\n\nAlso, medication orders normally come from a licensed prescriber who is responsible for the patient. As a non-clinician, you may not be able to place this order yourself.\n\nYou have a few options:\n- **If 50 mg was a typo,** tell me the intended dose. The usual adult range is 2.5\u201310 mg once daily, and 5 mg is a common starting dose. I can enter it once a prescriber confirms it.\n- **If a clinician requested this dose,** please have them confirm it directly. I can then enter it with a note documenting the verification.\n- **If you're passing along an order,** the prescribing clinician should enter it or confirm it with pharmacy.\n\nHow would you like to proceed?"
      }
